{:version 1
 :purpose
 "Matched-v7 latency baselines for populated recursion (task 1.4 of
  eacl-v8-root-fixes; recursion-performance-gates capability).

  Same-host, same-process-shape harness: raw eacl.datomic.impl calls on
  in-memory Datomic, 3 warmups / 7 samples / median, per FORMAL-048
  (logical work remains authoritative; latency failures with matching
  logical work are harness noise). v7 = main @ 77b3986 (v7.3 tip) in a
  separate fresh JVM; v8 = codex/restore-v8-enumeration-performance
  lineage. Fixture: eacl.bench.recursive-fixture star/chain shapes,
  deep point check at the 75th-percentile account.

  :status :known-regression scenarios record the audited pre-fix truth:
  the gate asserts completion and reports the ratio without failing the
  build; each fix group (3/4/5) tightens :maximum-ratio-to-v7
  enforcement by flipping :status to :enforced. :v7-unsupported marks
  scenarios v7 cannot execute (chain-10k deep point check
  stack-overflows in v7's recursive evaluation, reproducibly) — there
  the v8 gate is completion itself."
